  "user_request_original": "Design a dual-band anti-reflection coating on silicon substrate. Incident medium: air. Substrate: semi-infinite si. Coating stack: Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) | Ta2O5 (Gao) | SiO2 (Lemarchand) (12 layers, 6 pairs). Wavelength bands: 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm with equal weighting in objective. Incidence: 0 deg, unpolarized. Optimize all 12 layer thicknesses independently within 20-400 nm range. Objective: minimize weighted average reflectance with equal weight on both bands, plus minimize reflectance difference between bands. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, thicknesses_nm, and band-specific average reflectance and transmittance into silicon.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Optimize the 12 independent alternating Ta2O5 and SiO2 layer thicknesses (bounded 20–400 nm each) deposited on a semi-infinite silicon substrate in air at 0° normal incidence to minimize the mean reflectance in the 1260–1360 nm band and the 1530–1565 nm band with equal weights, thereby also balancing reflectance between the two bands.",
